---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="How We Rate Gear | ArcPoint Gear"
  description="ArcPoint Gear methodology for research reviews, field-tested reviews, spec analysis, and buying guides."
  canonical="/how-we-rate-gear"
>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "How We Rate Gear" }]} />
    <section class="page-hero" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Methodology</p>
      <h1>Every recommendation starts with the use case.</h1>
      <p>
        Our scores and recommendations are built around realistic missions, product specifications,
        category comparison, owner feedback signals, and clearly labeled editorial methods.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="method-grid" data-reveal>
      <article>
        <h2>Research Review</h2>
        <p>
          Based on product specifications, manufacturer documentation, category comparison, and
          owner feedback themes. This label does not claim hands-on testing.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h2>Field-Tested Review</h2>
        <p>
          Reserved for products evaluated through direct use. These articles should explain the
          test context, duration, conditions, and limitations.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h2>Spec Analysis</h2>
        <p>
          A technical breakdown of materials, weight, dimensions, feature sets, compatibility,
          and likely use-case fit.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h2>Buying Guide</h2>
        <p>
          A decision framework that helps readers understand product categories, tradeoffs, and
          shortlists without overstating certainty.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
